<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philip of Swabia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1177–1208</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philip of Swabia (1177–1208) was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> and King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> from 1198. After the death of his brother Henry VI, the Staufen party elected him king while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-welf">Welfs</a> elected Otto IV, starting a long civil war. Philip had gained the upper hand when he was murdered at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bamberg">Bamberg</a> in 1208 by Otto of Wittelsbach.</p></div>
